        "subject": "LU-6142 checkpatch: warn on GOTO() with a bare constant",
        "message": "LU-6142 checkpatch: warn on GOTO() with a bare constant\n\nGOTO() only logs its second argument, it never assigns it, so\nGOTO(label, -ENOMEM) reads like it sets the return value while\nactually discarding it and letting the target label return whatever\nwas there before. LU-4069 cleaned these out of the tree in 2013 and\nthey have accumulated again since, so warn at review time instead of\nfinding the next one the hard way. Existing occurrences are addressed\nseparately.\n\nGOTO(label, rc), GOTO(label, rc = -ENOMEM) and GOTO(label, 0) stay\nsilent, and RETURN(), which does return its argument, is not matched.\nA GOTO() wrapped onto a second line is matched too, but only the\nfirst one on a line, since more than one statement per line is an\nerror in its own right. The advice is worded conditionally because\nsome matching sites are in functions with no rc to assign to, and\nonly a plain constant is matched; the same trap spelled as an\nexpression is left for a follow-on.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I8b0d2cf5b326b8445cacc7387110314427a732de\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68280\nReviewed-by: James Simmons <jsimmons@infradead.org>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Arshad Hussain <arshad.hussain@aeoncomputing.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\n"
      },
